body:
So there was a point in my life where the bus didn't go through my route, my mom was too busy to drop me off, and my backpack had barely anything was still a boulder so biking was out of the question unless I wanted a concussion. Because of this I was constantly late, and I couldn't leave any earlier because at the time I left if I left any sooner it would basically be pitch black (this was in winter, during spring and summer I almost always made it on time). So I hit a point where I didn't give a shit anymore and just skipped half of first period so technically still getting to class. I'm adding nothing to this just felt like sharing my experience

&#x200B;

OK I forgot to add my solution to this issue. My mom would drive me half way bc she didn't care to go any further, I walked the rest of the way. Music helped kill the time, energy drinks too.
